messages:
Ava: Quick heads up 1: I uploaded a fresh draft of the product launch blog to the drive: https://drive.redwood.co/launch-draft-v2. Need fast reads on two items before we lock: benchmark claims (we have a ~2.5x figure in the subhead) and the webinar CTA routing + HubSpot params. Goal: finalize by tomorrow EOD and target publish Wed 9am PT.

Priya: On benchmark review. Can you paste the small-method blurb here so I can sanity check wording?

Ava: Sure. Blurb: "Internal benchmark vs baseline serving config; avg request ~120 tokens; continuous batching + prefix KV cache enabled. Observed up to 2.5x lower token cost in our tests, with comparable quality on our internal eval set."

Jon: Id rather hedge it: "up to 2.5x lower token cost in our benchmarks" + link to methodology. Legal prefers hedging.

Lina: Also please add a quick parenthetical on the eval composition (mix of long-form generation and short retrieval prompts). Makes the context clearer for readers.

Ava: Will edit to: "up to 2.5x lower token cost in our benchmarks using continuous batching + KV prefix caching (see methodology)." Adding a small footnote to the methodology doc.

Marco: Re: webinar CTA routing: recommend splitting lead flows: (A) live attendees -> immediate follow-up (slides + demo invite), (B) registrants who didn't attend -> nurture + on-demand replay, (C) blog clicks w/o webinar interest -> general inbound. That determines HubSpot workflows.

Ava: Can you paste the HubSpot snippet you want in the CTA code? I'll drop it into CMS action.

Marco: Pasting pseudocode below:

```
// HubSpot CTA routing for blog
if (event === 'webinar_attend') {
  hubspot.workflow = 'launch_live_attendees';
  utm_campaign = 'dedicated_launch_live';
} else if (event === 'webinar_register_no_show') {
  hubspot.workflow = 'launch_replay_nurture';
  utm_campaign = 'dedicated_launch_replay';
} else {
  hubspot.workflow = 'launch_general_inbound';
  utm_campaign = 'dedicated_launch_blog';
}
// always add tag: source=launch-blog
```

Ava: Nice. I'll include the block and add the source tag and UTM defaults (utm_source=blog, utm_medium=post).

Priya: Small bench tweak: please include p50/p95 latency numbers in a bulleted list so its scannable. Also say number of requests (10k) the medians are computed from.

Ava: Adding bullets: p50 = 120 ms, p95 = 420 ms (median across 10k requests). Also note token average and that batching was enabled.

Jon: @LegalBot can you do a quick pass on the hedged phrase + the methodology link? We need to ensure no unsupported comparison claims.

LegalBot: Automated check: "up to" phrasing ok. Recommend linking to methodology and ensuring no named customers or confidential snippets are included. Add a short disclaimer: "Results may vary by workload."

Ava: Added the disclaimer and removed a sentence that referenced an internal customer example.

Lina: UX suggestion: primary button text = "Register for launch webinar"; secondary = "Read technical notes". On phones stack buttons vertically; put an inline replay link under the second paragraph for non-registrants.

Ava: Updated CTA texts and mobile stacking guidance in CMS editor. Added an inline replay link anchor under the second paragraph.

Marco: For HubSpot make sure we add UTM params for segmentation: utm_source=blog, utm_medium=post, utm_campaign=dedicated_launch_blog OR dedicated_launch_live depending. Also tag contact property: lead_source = "launch_blog".

Ava: Done. I added a small JSON snippet under CTA settings with utm keys and contact tags.

Ava: Publish checklist for @PublishBot: 1) final copy in CMS, 2) hero image uploaded to CDN (s3://cdn.redwood/launch/hero-v3.jpg), 3) HubSpot CTA/webhook configured, 4) social posts scheduled. Can you run a webhook smoke test at publish time and confirm?

PublishBot: Scheduled smoke test for 2026-06-03T16:00:00Z. I will post confirmation here once the test passes. :robot_face:

Priya: One last copy ask: can someone proof the first paragraph hero claim to avoid overpromising?

Ava: Editing hero headline to: "Cut inference cost without sacrificing production-ready latency" and moving the quant figure to the subhead. Pinging @Jon for a quick final read in 20m.

Jon: On it in 20. Also change "production-ready" -> consistency with other pages. Typo check.

PublishBot: Smoke webhook OK at 2026-06-03T16:02:12Z  test payload accepted and routed to workflow `launch_live_attendees`.

Jon: Final read done  headline + subhead good. Minor nit: change "our benchmarks" to "in our internal benchmarks" for clarity.

Ava: Updated copy and pushed final version to CMS. Thanks team  legal final signoff is in the doc. Planning to publish per schedule once signoff is confirmed. :party_parrot:
